{"type":"message","id":"066e2efe","parentId":"8fda7acc","timestamp":"2026-05-20T06:55:09.129Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the perception layer calls `self.fetcher.get_kline(symbol, market, interval, limit)` where interval is a string. Let me check the actual error more carefully.\n\nThe error was:\n```\nProvider itick kline failed for US:CRCL: 'KlineInterval' object has no attribute 'get'\n```\n\nWait, this is confusing. The error says `'KlineInterval' object has no attribute 'get'`, which suggests that `KlineInterval` is being treated as an instance rather than a class, or that `ITICK_MAP` is somehow returning a KlineInterval instance instead of a dict.\n \nLooking at the iTick provider's `get_kline` method at line 824, I'm wondering if there's a shadowing issue where a local parameter is using the same name `k_type` and masking the class attribute. Let me trace through the iTick code more carefully to see where the dict lookup is actually failing.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c0e5747e87094bd3a0febbec","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/workspace/projects/workspace/chanlun-agent/data/finance_fetcher/finance_fetcher.py","limit":60,"offset":820}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":360,"output":458,"cacheRead":81984,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":82802,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779260095380}}
{"type":"message","id":"7b2472dc","parentId":"066e2efe","timestamp":"2026-05-20T06:55:09.137Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c0e5747e87094bd3a0febbec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"        except (KeyError, ValueError) as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Failed to parse iTick quote: {e}\")\n            return None\n    \n    def get_kline(self, code: str, region: str, k_type: str = \"101\", limit: int = 100) -> List[KlineBar]:\n        \"\"\"\n        获取K线数据\n        \n        Args:\n            code: 股票代码\n            region: 市场区域\n            k_type: K线类型 (1=1分钟, 5=5分钟, 15=15分钟, 30=30分钟, 60=1小时, 101=日线, 102=周线, 103=月线)\n            limit: 返回数量\n            \n        Returns:\n            List[KlineBar]\n        \"\"\"\n        # 缓存日线24小时，其他60秒\n        is_daily = k_type == \"101\"\n        cache_ttl = 86400 if is_daily else 60\n        cache_key = f\"itick_kline_{region}_{code}_{k_type}_{limit}\"\n        \n        cached = self.cache.get(cache_key)\n        if cached:\n            return cached\n        \n        data = self._make_request(\"stock/kline\", {\n            \"region\": region,\n            \"code\": code,\n            \"kType\": k_type,\n            \"limit\": min(limit, 500)  # 最多500条\n        })\n        \n        if not data:\n            return []\n        \n        bars = []\n        try:\n            items = data if isinstance(data, list) else data.get('data', [])\n            for item in items:\n                bar = KlineBar(\n                    symbol=code,\n                    market=region,\n                    timestamp=item.get('t', item.get('timestamp', '')),\n                    open=float(item.get('o', 0)),\n                    high=float(item.get('h', 0)),\n                    low=float(item.get('l', 0)),\n                    close=float(item.get('c', item.get('ld', 0))),\n                    volume=int(item.get('v', 0)),\n                    interval=k_type,\n                    source=\"iTick\"\n                )\n                bars.append(bar)\n            \n            self.cache.set(cache_key, bars, cache_ttl)\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Failed to parse iTick kline: {e}\")\n        \n        return bars\n    \n\n[1481 more lines in file. Use offset=880 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779260109134}}
