{"type":"message","id":"1477d087","parentId":"b05da405","timestamp":"2026-05-20T09:13:36.323Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me give a summary. The key remaining item is to configure the bot to receive messages (event subscription), not just send. The current setup can send messages but can't receive @mentions. That requires configuring the Feishu event subscription.\n\nBut actually, the ChanlunAgent is integrated as a Skill within the existing OpenClaw bot. So the existing bot already receives messages. The question is whether ChanlunAgent can be invoked through the existing bot's message handling.\n\nLet me think about this... The existing OpenClaw bot already receives messages and can invoke skills. So when someone @'s the bot with \"分析 CRCL\", the bot should be able to recognize this as a ChanlunAgent skill invocation and run the analysis.\n\n\nThe skill metadata is already in place with the right trigger keywords, so OpenClaw should automatically route messages like \"分析 CRCL\" or \"分析AAPL\" to the ChanlunAgent skill. I'll test this by sending a message to the bot and seeing if it gets routed correctly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"**飞书凭证已就绪！** 现在测试通过现有 Bot 调用 ChanlunAgent："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_030c06ae22d54281a3e92012","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/projects/workspace/chanlun-agent && python3 ChanlunAgent.py -c 分析 -a CRCL 2>&1 | grep -v \"^2026\\|WARNING\\|INFO\"","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":207,"output":529,"cacheRead":91712,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":92448,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779268406032}}
